WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.750
In Central Asia, NASA says, the desert
was made to bloom by irrigation.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.810
From the 1960s, cotton and other
crops spread across the dry land.

3
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.490
Nearby lay the Aral Sea, once
the world's 4th-largest lake.

4
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.510
In 2014, the eastern lobe of the
South Aral disappeared completely.

5
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.970
And fields turned salty.

6
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.630
How can watering a desert damage it?

7
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.970
Too much fertiliser?

8
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:32.210
In this mission, you'll see why a dry
soil is not necessarily an infertile one,

9
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.050
and where desert farms find water.

10
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.210
Then you'll weigh who controls the land,
with evidence from herders in Botswana

11
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:39.890
and Kenya.

12
00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:45.090
Your mission: explain how watering
Central Asia's desert damaged it.
